<title>FRANCE: France Telecom, CEA set to buy SGS Thomson stake.</title>
<headline>France Telecom, CEA set to buy SGS Thomson stake.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>France Telecom said that if Lagardere Groupe planned to sell the 20 percent stake in SGS-Thomson Microelectronics NV held by Thomson-CSF, it and state-owned CEA Industrie were ready to buy.</p>
<p>&quot;We have a shareholders pact. If Mr Lagardere wants to sell then we are ready to deliver on our promise and buy,&quot; a spokesman said, adding that the price of the transaction would be below today's market price.</p>
<p>The spokesman said France Telecom, which at the moment has 20 percent of Thomson SA, would not participate in the state's planned 11 billion franc capital increase of Thomson.</p>
</text>
